  "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=8x,$ we first replace $y$ with $8x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{(8x)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{64{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ -3{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=8x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
